</table>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This pattern has implications for the SCR metric. Its small-<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> ablation protocol is sensitive to feature <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">concentration</span> of the spurious attribute, rather than to whether the attribute has been removed from the representation. Architectural changes that concentrate rather than redistribute the attribute can produce SCR regressions even when the architecture achieves better disentanglement.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Autointerp drill-down</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On BatchTopK, the bottleneck reduces the mean autointerp score from .869 to .857 (<math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>1.2 pp), while Matryoshka is unchanged (.865 vs. .865). We run a per-feature drill-down to localize this regression, averaging per-latent scores across 3 random seeds (each sampling 1000 features from the same dictionary).</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A7.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix G Autointerp drill-down ‣ Decompose Sparsely Where You Should, Absorb Densely Where You Should Not" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> bins features by fire rate and compares mean autointerp score between <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}24</annotation></semantics></math> on BatchTopK. The regression is small and distributed across bins rather than concentrated in any single fire-rate population. The largest per-bin delta (<math id="A7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>1.8 pp) occurs in the [0.01, 0.05] range. The two residual dense latents with fire rate <math id="A7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0.3</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}24</annotation></semantics></math> score .464, but represent only 2 of 2794 sampled features.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A7.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A7.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mean autointerp score by fire-rate bin on BatchTopK (<math id="A7.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}0</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A7.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}24</annotation></semantics></math>, 3-seed average). The <math id="A7.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>1.2 pp overall regression is distributed across bins. <math id="A7.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> = number of unique features sampled in that bin.</span></figcaption>
